a1b-d5e4c0bbca87" 13194139534819 true] [17592186312118 1145 "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312120 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312121 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312122 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312123 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186312124 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1041 "selection" 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1104 #edb/ref 17592186312121 13194139534819 true] [17592186312119 1110 #uuid "c443ab42-5f80-5b3e-b39f-f166702fbf8e" 13194139534819 true] [17592186312120 1034 "The plane is undefined" 13194139534819 true] [17592186312120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534819 true] [17592186312120 1111 #uuid "2ea2ac09-96b1-5b6b-af83-440a89eab687" 13194139534819 true] [17592186312121 